    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d86">

                <pb facs="0219" n="163" sameAs="frus:frus1876/pg163"/>

                <head>No. 85.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Nicholas
                            Fish to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1876-09-19"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 19,
                        1876</date>. (Received October 12.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 483.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith a copy
                    and translation of a correspondence between Count Ledochowski and Pastor Brenk.
                    The <pb facs="0220" n="164" xml:id="pg164"/> Archbishop thus seeks to set the
                    Prussian laws at defiance and to exercise his jurisdiction within the territory
                    of Prussia.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>NICHOLAS FISH.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d86-a1.xml" xpointer="d86-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
